   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">Total depreciation expense was $<ix:nonFraction id="c141655637" contextRef="d_2025-01-01_2025-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.7</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million and $<ix:nonFraction id="c141655638" contextRef="d_2024-01-01_2024-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-5">0.6</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million for the years ended <em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2025 </em>and <em style="font: inherit;">2024</em>, respectively. Depreciation expense is included within cost of goods sold and selling, general and administrative expense in the Consolidated Statements of Operations.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <ix:exclude>
    <div class="PGFTR" style="text-align: center; width: 100%">
